cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "QHE-EJP: Reproducible Computational Introduction to the Integer Quantum Hall Effect"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Rocha
    given-names: Gabriel W. C.
version: 0.6.0
date-released: 2026-07-06
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/GabrielWendell/qhe-ejp"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible scientific-computing and teaching repository connecting Berry
  curvature and Chern-number calculations to quantitative bulk-boundary
  correspondence in the Harper-Hofstadter model. The current tagged release
  contains the validated static topology and edge-physics workflow; time-domain
  chiral dynamics remains a planned extension.
keywords:
  - quantum Hall effect
  - topological phases
  - Berry curvature
  - Chern number
  - Harper-Hofstadter model
  - computational physics
  - physics education
